},"authors":[{"full_name":"Grazzini, M."},{"full_name":"Kallweit, S."},{"full_name":"Wiesemann, M."}]},"raw_refs":[{"schema":"text","source":"CDS","value":"[63] M. Grazzini, S. Kallweit, and M. Wiesemann, “Fully differential NNLO computations with MATRIX”, Eur. Phys. J. C 78 (2018) 537, doi:10.1140/epjc/s10052-018-5771-7, arXiv:1711.06631."}],"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1636973"}},{"reference":{"dois":["10.1016/j.nuclphysbps.2010.08.011"],"arxiv_eprint":"1007.3492","label":"64","publication_info":{"journal_volume":"205","artid":"206","year":2010,"page_start":"206","journal_title":"Nucl.Phys.B Proc.Suppl."},"title":{"title":"MCFM for the Tevatron and the LHC"},"misc":["10"],"authors":[{"full_name":"Campbell, J.M."},{"full_name":"Ellis, R.K."}]},"raw_refs":[{"schema":"text","source":"CDS","value":"[64] J. M. Campbell and R. K. Ellis, “MCFM for the Tevatron and the LHC”, Nucl. Phys. B Proc. Suppl. 205-206 (2010) 10, doi:10.1016/j.nuclphysbps.2010.08.011, arXiv:1007.3492."}],"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/861954"}},{"reference":{"collaborations":["CMS Collaboration"],"dois":["10.1088/1748-0221/14/07/P07004"],"arxiv_eprint":"1903.06078","label":"65","publication_info":{"journal_volume":"14","artid":"P07004","year":2019,"journal_title":"JINST"},"title":{"title":"Performance of missing transverse momentum reconstruction in proton-proton collisions at √ s = 13 TeV using the CMS detector"},"misc":["W+ W- The","diboson W+W- analysis targets leptonic W boson decays, W+W- → ℓ+ℓ-νℓνℓ with ℓ = e, µ. The background composition depends strongly on the lepton-flavour final state: sameflavour events (ee, µµ) are dominated by Drell-Yan production, while different-flavour events (eµ) are dominated by top-quark processes. To maximize sensitivity to SMEFT effects, only the different-flavour (eµ) category is considered, further split by jet multiplicity (Njets = 0, 1). The analysis uses the full 2016-2018 CMS dataset, corresponding to an integrated luminosity of 138 fb-1. Events are preselected using single-lepton or dilepton triggers, requiring at least one isolated electron or muon, or two isolated leptons (electrons and/or muons), respectively. Leptons are further selected offline using tight MVA-based identification [51-53] and isolation criteria, together with track-based constraints consistent with the primary vertex. Jets are reconstructed with the anti-kT [54, 55] algorithm using a distance parameter of R = 0.4, and are required to satisfy p j T > 30 GeV and |ηj| < 4.7. The pmiss T is computed with the PUPPI algorithm [56, 57]. Jets from b quark fragmentation are identified among jets with p"],"authors":[{"full_name":"Diboson, A."}]},"raw_refs":[{"schema":"text","source":"CDS","value":"[65] CMS Collaboration, “Performance of missing transverse momentum reconstruction in proton-proton collisions at √ s = 13 TeV using the CMS detector”, JINST 14 (2019) P07004, doi:10.1088/1748-0221/14/07/P07004, arXiv:1903.06078. A Diboson W+ W− The diboson W+W− analysis targets leptonic W boson decays, W+W− → ℓ+ℓ−νℓνℓ with ℓ = e, µ. The background composition depends strongly on the lepton-flavour final state: sameflavour events (ee, µµ) are dominated by Drell–Yan production, while different-flavour events (eµ) are dominated by top-quark processes. To maximize sensitivity to SMEFT effects, only the different-flavour (eµ) category is considered, further split by jet multiplicity (Njets = 0, 1). The analysis uses the full 2016–2018 CMS dataset, corresponding to an integrated luminosity of 138 fb−1 . Events are preselected using single-lepton or dilepton triggers, requiring at least one isolated electron or muon, or two isolated leptons (electrons and/or muons), respectively. Leptons are further selected offline using tight MVA-based identification [51–53] and isolation criteria, together with track-based constraints consistent with the primary vertex. Jets are reconstructed with the anti-kT [54, 55] algorithm using a distance parameter of R = 0.4, and are required to satisfy p j T > 30 GeV and |ηj| < 4.7. The pmiss T is computed with the PUPPI algorithm [56, 57]. Jets from b quark fragmentation are identified among jets with p"}],"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1724943"}}],"number_of_pages":32,"referenced_authors_bais":["E.Stanecka.1","F.Colombo.2","Tom.Elliot.1","Souvik.Das.1","J.Thom.1","I.Marchesini.1","G.Chevenier.1","A.Strubig.1","H.Ito.8","R.A.Rojas.1","F.Noto.1","Christian.Schmitt.1","Angelos.Zografos.1","T.Kypreos.1","Y.T.Hsu.2","M.Lazarovits.1","A.Tcheremoukhine.1","T.M.Knight.1","M.Dragicevic.1","C.Sanzeni.1","J.Assahsah.1","S.Farinon.1","M.Hashemi.1","Jose.Pretel.1","Huaqiao.Zhang.1","C.Burgos.lazaro.2","G.Rakness.1","M.Gallinaro.1","Xin.Wu.1","A.Perez.Calero.Yzquierdo.1","W.Beaumont.1","A.C.Daniells.1","P.Atmasiddha.1","M.Atac.1","I.Chalupkova.1","E.Berry.1","J.Godlewski.1","Denise.Muller.1","B.Diab.1","Marten.Z.Barel.1","P.Lawson.1","I.De.Bruyn.1","M.Goncharov.1","J.W.Andrejkovic.1","Abigail.Warden.1","Arturo.Sanchez.1","M.Stoye.1","R.J.Sobie.1","Y.A.Rodina.1","F.Guillot.Vignot.1","Serhii.Cholak.1","I.Laflotte.1","Blair.Seidlitz.1","V.Bunichev.1","J.C.Williams.1","Y.Yu.61","M.Fahling.1","Tadeas.Petru.1","Ozgun.Kara.1","R.Malina.2","Robin.Nandi.1","S.Lammel.1","M.Trimpl.1","T.Barata.Monteiro.1","S.Ronchi.2","Arora.Arora.1","Ruo.Yu.Shang.1","A.Borkar.1","G.F.Rzehorz.1","L.Wiens.1","C.Rangel.Smith.1","E.R.Vandewall.1","C.E.Perez.Lara.1","Y.I.Skovpen.1","S.Schulz.2","W.F.Mader.1","H.Nguyen.1","J.F.Benitez.1","Iza.Veliscek.1","F.Romano.1","J.P.Teixeira.1","Y.Zoccarato.1","Laurent.Forthomme.1","M.Hansen.1","H.W.K.Cheung.1","A.Solano.1","C.Verollet.1","C.Marchica.1","I.Soric.1","H.Gray.1","Z.Duan.3","P.Katsoulis.1","M.Donadelli.1","A.Datta.23","R.Del.Burgo.1","T.Gillam.1","E.von.Toerne.1","D.J.A.Cockerill.1","M.Capua.1","B.Kansal.1","Yun.Xiu.Ye.1","M.Rijssenbeek.1","M.Salvatore.1","M.B.Santos.1","H.Seo.1","K.T.Greif.1","P.Dehm.1","Jorg.Schi