tt.1","A.Elliott.Peisert.1","Jing.Chen.1","M.Niedziela.1","J.S.Kim.1","H.K.Chung.1","N.Panyam.1","Kyle.Amirie.1","S.D.Lawlor.1","F.M.Giorgi.2","H.Larsen.1","D.Seith.1","A.Usanova.1","M.Bercher.1","Micael.Verissimo.De.Araujo.1","Anna.Ivina.1","M.D.Werner.1","T.Dorigo.1","M.G.Pia.1","Arthur.Kraus.1","Yue.Xu.1","A.Tsirigotis.1","Badr.eddine.Ngair.1","Berare.Gokturk.1","Konstantin.Mauer.1","A.S.Ayan.1","A.Adolf.2","K.Zoch.1","N.Valls.1","R.Guida.2","James.Inglis.1","A.Coccaro.1","A.Jaiswal.2","Kelci.Mohrman.1","S.M.Turchikhin.1","P.Levchenko.1","M.Guchait.1","I.A.Hadjiagapiou.1","D.Krofcheck.1","R.G.Thomas.1","E.M.Gasanov.1","S.Stoenchev.1","J.P.Peigneux.12","M.Weinberg.1","Manabu.Togawa.1","M.Moreno.Llacer.1","K.Yamauchi.2","J.Robles.1","D.N.Laroze.Navarrete.1","W.Leight.1","E.Sideras.Haddad.1","Jose.de.Jesus.Hernandez.Orduna.1","H.Musheghyan.1"],"collaborations":[{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/experiments/1108642"},"value":"CMS"}],"inspire_categories":[{"term":"Experiment-HEP","source":"cds"}],"accelerator_experiments":[{"legacy_name":"CERN-LHC-CMS","record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/experiments/1108642"}}],"author_count":0,"public_notes":[{"source":"CDS","value":"Preliminary results"}],"control_number":3185630,"earliest_date":"2026-07-30","document_type":["note"],"texkeys":["CMS:2026abp"],"abstracts":[{"source":"CDS","value":"A search for new physics in electroweak multiboson production is performed through a statistical combination of ten CMS measurements using proton-proton collision data collected at $\\sqrt{s}=13$ TeV during 2016--2018, corresponding to an integrated luminosity of 138 fb$^{-1}$. The combination encompasses six vector boson scattering channels: same-sign $\\mathrm{WW}$ production in fully leptonic and $\\ell\\tau_\\mathrm{h}$ final states, opposite-sign $\\mathrm{WW}$, $\\mathrm{WZ}$, and two VBS channels with a hadronically decaying vector boson ($\\mathrm{WV}$ and $\\mathrm{ZV}$); two vector boson fusion channels ($\\mathrm{Wjj}$ and $\\mathrm{Zjj}$), inclusive $\\mathrm{W^+W^-}$ diboson production, and triboson VVV (no $\\gamma$) production. Within the standard model effective field theory framework, potential contributions from physics beyond the standard model are parameterized in terms of six CP-even bosonic dimension-six operators of the Warsaw basis: $\\mathcal{O}_{W}$, $\\mathcal{O}_{HW}$, $\\mathcal{O}_{HWB}$, $\\mathcal{O}_{H\\square}$, $\\mathcal{O}_{HB}$, and $\\mathcal{O}_{HD}$. Their effects are introduced through event-by-event reweighting of leading-order Monte Carlo simulations, enabling a consistent propagation of EFT effects to detector level with a consistent treatment of systematic uncertainties. Constraints on the associated Wilson coefficients are extracted using a binned profile likelihood fit, in scenarios ranging from individual coefficients to the fully profiled six-dimensional fit. No significant deviations from the standard model are observed. The combination improves substantially upon any individual analysis and constitutes the first detector-level combination of direct EFT measurements targeting bosonic dimension-six operators at the LHC.","abstract_source_suggest":{"input":"CDS"}}],"titles":[{"title":"Constraints on Effective Field Theory operators from multiboson production measurements at $\\sqrt{s} = 13$ TeV"},{"source":"CDS","title":"SMP SMEFT combination"}],"external_system_identifiers":[{"schema":"CDS","value":"2967655"}],"corporate_author":["The CMS Collaboration"],"core":true,"imprints":[{"date":"2026-07-30"}],"_oai":{"sets":["Literature"],"id":"oai:inspirehep.net:3185630","updated":"2026-08-26T14:33:33.136453"},"curated":true},"id":"3185630"}],"total":1},"links":{"self":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=reportnumber%3ACMS-PAS-SMP-25-002&size=10&page=1","bibtex":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=reportnumber%3ACMS-PAS-SMP-25-002&size=10&page=1&format=bibtex","latex-eu":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=reportnumber%3ACMS-PAS-SMP-25-002&size=10&page=1&format=latex-eu","latex-us":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=reportnumber%3ACMS-PAS-SMP-25-002&size=10&page=1&format=latex-us","json":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=reportnumber%3ACMS-PAS-SMP-25-002&size=10&page=1&format=json","json-expanded":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=reportnumber%3ACMS-PAS-SMP-25-002&size=10&page=1&format=json-expanded","cv":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=reportnumber%3ACMS-PAS-SMP-25-002&size=10&page=1&format=cv"}}